{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-120119-r4615172","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Meat Masala","sourcePageId":120119,"sourceRevision":"4615172","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:31:20Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Meat%20Masala&oldid=4615172","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:29.501Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for spice mixes","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using whole cumin","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"7b1822c71037de1494308f9303d583295cd272cff0732be754e7a98daf025243","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Spice mix recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Spices and herbs|Spices]]\n\n'''Meat masala''' is a spice mix used in [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Keralan cuisine]], typically as a [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinade]] for various types of [[Cookbook:Meat|meat]], especially [[Cookbook:Mutton|mutton]].\n\nMeat masala can either be rubbed onto pieces of meat as a dry powder mix, or combined with [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]] to make a paste that more easily coats the meat. Once coated, the meat should be left to marinate for at least 20 minutes, but preferably up to 2 hours, before cooking.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 50 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] whole dried [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|chillies]]\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander seed]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Pepper|black peppercorn]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin seed]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard seed]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* 12 [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom seed]]\n* 2 short pieces of [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Toast the chillies, coriander, peppercorn, cumin, and mustard in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]].\n# Grind all ingredients to a powder.\n# Store in a glass jar with a tight-fitting lid.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for spice mixes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Meat Masala","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"50 g whole dried chillies","sourceText":"50 g whole dried chillies","amountText":"50 g whole dried chillies","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"100 g coriander seed","sourceText":"100 g coriander seed","amountText":"100 g coriander seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tbsp black peppercorn","sourceText":"2 tbsp black peppercorn","amountText":"2 tbsp black peppercorn","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tsp cumin seed","sourceText":"1 tsp cumin seed","amountText":"1 tsp cumin seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 tsp mustard seed","sourceText":"1 tsp mustard seed","amountText":"1 tsp mustard seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tsp turmeric powder","sourceText":"1 tsp turmeric powder","amountText":"1 tsp turmeric powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"12 cloves","sourceText":"12 cloves","amountText":"12 cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"¼ tsp cardamom seed","sourceText":"¼ tsp cardamom seed","amountText":"¼ tsp cardamom seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 short pieces of cinnamon","sourceText":"2 short pieces of cinnamon","amountText":"2 short pieces of cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Toast the chillies, coriander, peppercorn, cumin, and mustard in a frying pan.","sourceText":"Toast the chillies, coriander, peppercorn, cumin, and mustard in a frying pan.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Grind all ingredients to a powder.","sourceText":"Grind all ingredients to a powder.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Store in a glass jar with a tight-fitting lid.","sourceText":"Store in a glass jar with a tight-fitting lid.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:120119","recordId":"wikibooks-120119-r4615172","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4615172","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Meat%20Masala&oldid=4615172","sourceSha256":"7b1822c71037de1494308f9303d583295cd27